{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L94-L100","doc":"**Integer-exponent selection rule.** The Borel exponent `b = κ(σ) − κ(σ′)` is `0`\n(the only integer value it takes) **iff** the two connections lie on the same side of\ntriviality — both trivial or both non-trivial. The A_ω ray (both non-trivial) is on\nthe integer branch; every `σ₀`-ray is on the half-integer branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_three_halves_needs_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_three_halves_needs_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**The weight `3/2` requires a trivial endpoint.** `b = ±3/2` can occur only on a\n`σ₀ ↔ (non-trivial)` ray — a *different* singularity than A_ω (which is\ngeometric↔conjugate). Formalizes why testing `β = 3/2` against the\ngeometric–conjugate ladder is a category error. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_aomega_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_aomega_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The A_ω ray has integer characteristic exponent `b = 0`.** Both endpoints of the\nA_ω ray — geometric `σ₁` and conjugate `σ̄₁` — have weight `0`, so its Borel exponent\nis `0 ∈ ℤ`. Hence the A_ω Stokes constant is an **integer** (the DT/BPS `3d`-index\ncount, GGM Conj. 2), not a half-integer-weight modular quantity. This is the correct\nreplacement for the refuted `β = 3/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff_mem","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L70-L74","doc":"**The Borel exponent of any `4₁` Stokes ray is `0` or `±3/2`.** These are the only\nvalues of `κ(σ) − κ(σ′)` — the discrete selection: no continuous `β` to fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.kappa_eq_three_halves_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.kappa_eq_three_halves_iff","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L65-L68","doc":"**`σ₀` is the unique weight-`3/2` connection** (GZ eq. 3.7). The `3/2` belongs to\nthe trivial connection alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.weightDiff","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L59-L63","doc":"The **Borel characteristic exponent** of a Stokes ray joining `σ, σ′` is the\nweight difference `b = κ(σ) − κ(σ′)` (GZ eq. 3.7–3.8: the completed series carries the\nautomorphy factor `|cℏ|^{κ(σ)}`, so a ray's exponent is the difference of endpoint\nweights). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.kappa","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.kappa","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L50-L57","doc":"**Garoufalidis–Zagier representation weight** `κ` (2111.06645 eq. 3.7):\n`κ(σ₀) = 3/2` for the trivial connection, `0` for every non-trivial connection. The\n`3/2` is the automorphy-factor exponent of the Kashaev `N^{3/2}` prefactor — a\ndiscrete, representation-indexed weight, **not** a Borel loggamma index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.instFintypeFlatConn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.instFintypeFlatConn","kind":"instance","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.instDecidableEqFlatConn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.instDecidableEqFlatConn","kind":"instance","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma1bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma1bar","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma1","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn.sigma0","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GZWeightSelection.FlatConn","kind":"inductive","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GZWeightSelection.lean#L38-L46","doc":"The three flat connections of the figure-eight (`4₁`) parabolic character variety\nthat carry the resurgent structure: the **trivial** connection `sigma0` (`σ₀`, whose\ncolumn is the Kashaev invariant in the Habiro ring), the **geometric** connection\n`sigma1` (`σ₁`), and its complex **conjugate** `sigma1bar` (`σ̄₁`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}